  "clarifyingQuestions": [
    "Is one approval enough when changes were also requested earlier?",
    "Which artifacts prove agent work is reviewable?",
    "Should pending check status count as failing for required checks?"
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "Require code-owner approvals by path.",
    "Add stale-review invalidation after new commits.",
    "Attach blockers to user-facing PR status."
  ],
  "followUpGuide": [
    "For code owners, map changed paths to owner groups and require one approval per group.",
    "",
    "For stale reviews, define whether a new head invalidates an approval, then compare review commit SHA against head SHA. If consuming review history, first reduce it to each reviewer's effective current state; the base problem intentionally doesn't do that.",
    "",
    "For agent PRs, artifacts should include diff, tests, run log, cost, and screenshots when UI changed."
  ],
  "complexityAnalysis": [
    "- Building check map. Time: O(c), where c is check count. Space: O(c).",
    "- Review and artifact scans. Time: O(r + a + k), where k is the required-check list length. Space: O(r + a) for the review-state list and artifact set.",
    "- Sorting blockers. Time: O(b log b). Space: O(b), where b is blocker count."
  ],
  "solutionGuide": [
    "Index required data first, then collect string blockers and sort at the end.",
    "",
    "```python",
    "def pr_blockers(checks: list[dict], reviews: list[dict], artifacts: list[str], required_checks: list[str]) -> list[str]:",
    "    blockers = []",
    "    by_check = {check.get(\"name\"): check.get(\"status\") for check in checks}",
    "    for name in required_checks:",
    "        if name not in by_check:",
    "            blockers.append(f\"missing_check:{name}\")",
    "        elif by_check[name] != \"passed\":",
    "            blockers.append(f\"failing_check:{name}\")",
    "    states = [review.get(\"state\") for review in reviews]",
    "    if \"approved\" not in states:",
    "        blockers.append(\"approval_required\")",
    "    if \"changes_requested\" in states:",
    "        blockers.append(\"changes_requested\")",
    "    artifact_set = set(artifacts)",
    "    for artifact in (\"diff\", \"tests\"):",
    "        if artifact not in artifact_set:",
    "            blockers.append(f\"missing_artifact:{artifact}\")",
    "    return sorted(blockers)",
    "```"
  ]
}
